# Netlify redirects for the single-page app. Vite copies this file into dist. Build settings and
# headers are in netlify.toml; redirects are defined only here. Rules are read top to bottom and
# the first match wins. Neither rule is forced, so a file that really exists (a script, a font,
# the favicon) is always served as is.

# Build files carry a content hash in their names. A request for one that no longer exists, such
# as an old tab asking for the previous deploy's chunk, must get a real 404 rather than
# index.html, or the browser would try to run HTML as JavaScript.
/assets/*    /404.html      404

# SPA fallback. /gemini, /chatgpt, /whatsapp and the rest pick the platform in the app; they are
# not files, so they are answered with index.html and a 200.
/*           /index.html    200
